<ArticleLayout
  title="Water, Sanitation & Community Health"
  description="Safe drinking water and sustainable menstrual health access in Sierra Leone."
>
  <p>
    Clean water and basic health access shape everything else a
    community can build. This area combines commercial and social
    models to make both more available.
  </p>

  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <p>
    RiverSafe is a commercial drinking-water treatment and bottling
    plant, built as a social business that creates local jobs across
    bottling, machine operation and sales while extending access to
    safe drinking water.
  </p>
  <p>
    A sustainable menstrual health project distributes reusable cups
    and discs through nurse-led training, paired with a rural sales
    model that creates income opportunities for local women alongside
    improving health access.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    Both projects are built as social businesses first: they need to
    cover their own running costs over time, not depend on permanent
    subsidy, which is what makes them realistic to sustain once initial
    funding ends.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
